<title>HONG KONG: Vanda buys HK-China system integrator.</title>
<headline>Vanda buys HK-China system integrator.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vanda Systems &amp; Communications Holdings Ltd said on Monday it had acquired an 80 percent stake in computer system integrator TMS China (H.K.) Ltd.</p>
<p>TMS China has about 150 customers, mainly comprising Japanese-funded enterprises in Hong Kong and China, and its service network based in Beijing, Shanghai and Hong Kong covered almost all of China, Vanda said in a statement.</p>
<p>Its acquisition would further expand Vanda's customer base, the computer system integrator and distributor said.</p>
<p>Financial details were not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
